From e2f3eca145dbfcf0bdd04620705d2fee5e4c2aa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:57:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/32] test(qsa): correct the selection width --
 qsa_token_topk IS the budget

The byte budget was pinned at a 515-column selection (budget // ratio + ratio - 1).
It is 2051: kv_cache_configurator.py:1936 passes qsa_token_topk=qsa_profile.budget
(2048) and qsa_kv_pool.py:125 derives qsa_block_topk = token_topk // ratio (512),
so the 512 is the BLOCK top-k; the gather sees the expanded token selection,
qsa/kernel.py:211 final_topk = token_topk + ratio - 1. Page-aligned that is 33
pages of 64 = a 2112-row run per query row, not 576.

Restated at B3c-4 (max_bs 4, kv heads 2, head_dim 256, bf16):
  per QSA backend instance, packed-KV k+v at W=8 = 132 MiB (was stated 36)
  unshared across tiers {1,3,5,7}: 20 instances, 2560 MiB workspace + 858 MiB gather
  shared: 128 + 132 MiB  ->  3158 MiB recovered overall,
  2675 MiB across the three EXTRA tiers = 105354 bf16 KV tokens at 26 KB.

This now matches the executor's measured per-state mem= lines, which the old
numbers did not: predicted unshared steps=1 = 0.31 GiB [measured 0.35], steps=5 =
1.01 GiB [measured 1.10], the residual being graph-pool growth and the static
input/metadata buffers. Same correction applied to the GPU2 equivalence script,
which re-passes: 4 tiers plus an A->B->A interleave bitwise equal to private
scratch, 1 allocation of 138412032 bytes, peak 0.29 GiB, 5.1 s.
